-- title:
--   The canonical facet equivalence omits its label
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a nonnegative integer, and let $j\in\{0,\ldots,n\}$ label a vertex of the ordered $(n+1)$-vertex simplex. The canonical equivalence from vertex labels to increasing faces of size $n$ sends $j$ to the face omitting $j$:
--   $$
--   \Phi_n(j)=F_j.
--   $$
--   Here $F_j$ is the increasing embedding whose image is the complement of the singleton $\{j\}$.
